{"name":"First of July","hex":"#bce6ef","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"first","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Preceding all others of a series or kind; the ordinal of one; earliest.","Most eminent or exalted; most excellent; chief; highest."]},{"part":"Adverb","definitions":["Before anything else; firstly.","For the first time."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/first"}],"entries":[{"title":"July 1","blocks":[{"text":"July 1 is the 182nd day of the year in the Gregorian calendar; 183 days remain until the end of the year."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July_1"},{"title":"July","blocks":[{"text":"July is the seventh month of the year in the Julian and Gregorian calendars. Its length is 31 days. It was named by the Roman Senate in honour of Roman general and statesman Julius Caesar in 44 B.C., being the month of his birth. Before then it was called Quintilis, being the fifth month of the calendar that started with March."}],"link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/July"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f0/Ruby_gem.JPG/330px-Ruby_gem.JPG?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Ruby gemstone","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ARuby_gem.JPG"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/500px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg/1280px-Baker%27s_Larkspur_%285933879987%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/1/14/Bake